	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nConnects the board to a vehicle CAN bus: J1939 / FMS on trucks, OBD-II over CAN on cars, any 11/29-bit CAN up to 1 Mbit/s.\nU1001 turns the ESP32 CAN controller's 3.3 V logic (CAN_TX, CAN_RX) into the two bus wires CAN_H and CAN_L, and back.\nD1001 protects the bus pins; two solder jumpers set the 120 ohm termination and a hardware listen-only mode.\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\nCAN_H (bus): J1 pin 13 (twisted pair with CAN_L; bus ground on J1 pin 2)\nCAN_L (bus): J1 pin 5\nCAN_TX (in): from ESP32 GPIO33: what the board sends\nCAN_RX (out): to ESP32 GPIO15: what the bus carries\n+5V (in): transceiver supply (bus side), from the 5 V rail\n+3V3 (in): logic supply (VIO), from the 3.3 V regulator\nGND: ground\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 265 32.7)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "52352f7c-373b-5228-a0d9-9848ab2ca486")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 162.56 63.5)
		(end 231.14 116.84)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "ec6ad2fd-46c9-5882-aa76-5b1fcfdebb33")
	)
	(text "keep together on the PCB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 163.16 64.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a23dc8fe-765e-5158-a6a1-666e124015be")
	)
	(text "C1001 belongs to U1001 pin 3 (VCC, 5 V),\nC1002 to pin 5 (VIO, 3.3 V): each within\n2 mm of its pin, GND via beside its GND pad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 233.68 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cff4661a-6c6f-58ed-bf1a-16735c885883")
	)
	(text "D1001 is the first part after J1\n(pins 13 and 5): place it right at\nthe connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cd52b7cc-1858-582d-9967-245c002fd014")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nU1001: TJA1051T/3 high-speed CAN transceiver (ISO 11898-2). VCC = 5 V powers the bus driver, VIO = 3.3 V sets the logic level to the ESP32. CANH/CANL are rated +/-58 V, so a 12/24 V miswire is survived. Drawn mirrored: bus pins on the left.\nC1001: 100 nF decoupling for U1001 VCC (pin 3, +5V). Must sit at pin 3 on the PCB.\nC1002: 100 nF decoupling for U1001 VIO (pin 5, +3V3). Must sit at pin 5 on the PCB.\nD1001: SZNUP3105L bus protector: clamps surges on CAN_H and CAN_L to GND. 32 V working voltage, so it stays off on a 24 V system.\nR1001, JP1001: 120 ohm bus termination, only when the solder jumper JP1001 (TERM) is bridged. Open as delivered: a vehicle bus is already terminated at both ends; bridge it only when the board ends a bus (e.g. on the bench).\nJP1002: LISTEN-ONLY solder jumper. Bridged: S (pin 8) is tied to 3.3 V and the transceiver cannot transmit (hardware silent). Open (as delivered): S is pulled low inside the chip and the firmware chooses normal or listen-only mode."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 156 0)
		(size 155 24.5)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
